WEBVTT

00:00:00.212 --> 00:00:04.230
GhostOS · Dev agent — find bugs → patch → self-correct → test → pull request with a human in the loop for anything irreversible

00:00:04.316 --> 00:00:07.823
Task: “fix the failing tests in fixtures/buggy_repo and open a pull request”.

00:00:07.823 --> 00:00:12.889
Heads-up: this recording uses the scripted LLM provider so it's reproducible. Set ANTHROPIC_API_KEY for real reasoning.

00:00:12.889 --> 00:00:19.213
The repo is copied into an isolated sandbox and its test suite runs…

00:00:19.213 --> 00:00:21.870
3 failing tests. The Coder agent reads the failures and the source, then proposes a patch.

00:00:21.870 --> 00:00:25.094
Patch #1 fixes the separator and discount bugs… but the Verifier re-runs the suite: 1 test still fails.

00:00:25.094 --> 00:00:30.106
Self-correction: the Healer feeds that failure back, and the Coder finds the real root cause (padding width).

00:00:30.106 --> 00:00:32.262
12/12 tests green → commit on a new branch.

00:00:32.262 --> 00:00:36.768
Guardian: opening a pull request is irreversible, so GhostOS stops and asks a human.

00:00:36.769 --> 00:00:38.496
Approved ✓

00:00:38.496 --> 00:00:43.500
Done. PR drafted with diagnosis, verification and diff — the original repo was never touched.

00:00:43.500 --> 00:00:47.026
GhostOS — github.com/amartya1523/GhostOS-An-AI-That-Can-Operate-a-Computer
